		<orm:ModelNotes>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_E5DF183D-ADFC-4FFE-92B7-CD66DA15B6E1">
				<orm:Text>This subset of the FBM ORM model was chosen for testing purposes because
there are so many interesting patterns. This includes derived subtypes with
constraints, recursive derivation, projected objectifications, join constraints on
a link fact type, and other advanced combinations of inlined derivations.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_C179C5A4-6971-43A0-A1DB-47B6E409D5AE">
				<orm:Text>The JFE generators (model and rule) should be able to handle a derived
subtype like this without introducing the type.
1) The JFE generators need to defer to the supertype
2) The rule generator needs to delete all role players when the derivation is false.
3) Mandatory constraints from the subtype need to be enforced by the rule generator.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_A196A85C-965C-4362-8BD3-106C461E50E1" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_8A2EA1B6-1A6B-4271-92C4-CECC504A154C">
				<orm:Text>FreeFBM: this model was exported from FreeFBM. Everything in it is in
NORMA's form.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
		</orm:ModelNotes>
